      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Section 7 — Black-Box Core Components\n",
        "\n",
        "Section 6 described the black-box setting: we can submit messages and observe outputs, but cannot inspect the target model's weights or feature probabilities. This subsection prepares candidate words and tracks a query budget. It does not yet run an oracle attack.\n",
        "\n",
        "The frequency calculation is `freq(w) = sum over ham messages m of count(w, m)`. Read this as **“frequency of w equals the sum, over ham messages m, of the number of times w occurs in m.”** It counts repeated occurrences, not just messages that contain a word.\n",
        "\n",
        "We must use `train_text`, the raw cleaned message strings, with the aligned `y_train` labels. `X_train` in this notebook is already a sparse count matrix, so it is not the text corpus. The code checks alignment before pairing messages and labels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Query setup: these are counters and containers only; no target query is sent here.\n",
        "query_budget = 1000\n",
        "queries_used = 0\n",
        "query_log = []\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def extract_ham_word_freq(messages, labels, sample_size=500):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Count token occurrences in the first `sample_size` ham messages.\n",
        "\n",
        "    This follows the course's simple whitespace-tokenization example. The\n",
        "    messages and labels must remain aligned: entry i in each refers to the\n",
        "    same training example.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    message_values = np.asarray(messages, dtype=object)\n",
        "    label_values = np.asarray(labels)\n",
        "    if len(message_values) != len(label_values):\n",
        "        raise ValueError('messages and labels must have matching lengths')\n",
        "\n",
        "    ham_messages = message_values[label_values == 'ham']\n",
        "    limit = min(sample_size, len(ham_messages))\n",
        "    frequencies = {}\n",
        "    for message in ham_messages[:limit]:\n",
        "        for word in str(message).split():\n",
        "            # Keep 3-9 character tokens, as in HTB's example.\n",
        "            if 2 < len(word) < 10:\n",
        "                frequencies[word] = frequencies.get(word, 0) + 1\n",
        "    return frequencies\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def select_high_frequency_words(word_freq, max_words=100, min_freq=5):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return frequent words, ordered by count descending then alphabetically.\"\"\"\n",
        "    sorted_by_frequency = sorted(\n",
        "        word_freq.items(), key=lambda item: (-item[1], item[0])\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    # HTB's `count > min_freq` is strict: min_freq=5 requires at least 6.\n",
        "    return [word for word, count in sorted_by_frequency if count > min_freq][:max_words]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def merge_with_curated(top_words, additional_candidates=None):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Add a small conversational vocabulary and remove duplicates.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if additional_candidates is None:\n",
        "        additional_candidates = [\n",
        "            'ok', 'cos', 'ill', 'thats', 'later', 'said', 'ask', 'didnt',\n",
        "            'dont', 'doing', 'going', 'come', 'home', 'tomorrow', 'today',\n",
        "            'sorry', 'thanks', 'yeah', 'yes', 'sure', 'see', 'tell', 'know',\n",
        "            'think',\n",
        "        ]\n",
        "    # Set union guarantees one copy of each candidate.\n",
        "    return sorted(set(top_words) | set(additional_candidates))\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_candidate_vocabulary(\n",
        "    messages, labels, sample_size=500, max_words=100, min_freq=5,\n",
        "    additional_candidates=None,\n",
        "):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Build a reproducible candidate list from ham text plus curated terms.\"\"\"\n",
        "    word_freq = extract_ham_word_freq(messages, labels, sample_size=sample_size)\n",
        "    frequent_words = select_high_frequency_words(\n",
        "        word_freq, max_words=max_words, min_freq=min_freq\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    merged = merge_with_curated(frequent_words, additional_candidates)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Keep frequency-ranked words first; alphabetical order breaks ties.\n",
        "    return sorted(merged, key=lambda word: (-word_freq.get(word, 0), word))\n"
      ]
    },
