      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Read the helper pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "1. `extract_ham_word_freq` selects messages whose label is exactly `ham`, then counts whitespace-separated token occurrences. The first 500 ham rows are used, matching the course example; row order can bias this sample.\n",
        "2. `select_high_frequency_words` sorts by count and retains up to 100 words above the strict frequency threshold. `(-count, word)` means “largest count first; alphabetical order for ties.”\n",
        "3. `merge_with_curated` performs set union. In the final builder, unseen curated terms have frequency zero, so they come after observed terms. The final list may exceed 100 because the cap is applied before curated terms are added.\n",
        "\n",
        "This candidate pool comes from available ham training text. A true query-only attacker may not have that corpus; in that case, use another permitted source. Being common in ham is only a hypothesis about a word, not evidence that the hidden classifier will reward it."
